1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
*music*

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,680
Well, good morning, Canvas Community Church, family, friends.

3
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:39,940
So good to see you all for this first week of Advent.

4
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:42,900
I decided to rock the Bluey shirt.

5
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:44,740
Hopefully many of you got the announcement

6
00:00:44,740 --> 00:00:47,180
that some of my message is gonna be using

7
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:49,140
a Bluey episode as an illustration.

8
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:50,940
We'll get into that in just a little bit.

9
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:54,220
Last week, Kent started our Advent series

10
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:57,540
on the names of God given to us in the Bible.

11
00:00:57,540 --> 00:01:00,880
And when God reveals to us different names and titles,

12
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:04,280
it helps us better understand who he is

13
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:06,500
and how he relates to us.

14
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:09,860
Because the Bible is all about us being invited

15
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:11,480
into a relationship with God, amen?

16
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:15,680
So for the rest of our Advent,

17
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:19,500
we are going to look at a list of titles or names

18
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:23,060
that the prophet Isaiah gives God about Jesus

19
00:01:23,060 --> 00:01:24,180
before he comes.

20
00:01:24,180 --> 00:01:27,400
This was to prepare them so that they would recognize

21
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:28,560
when he arrived.

22
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:31,880
So Marissa and I do this on a regular basis

23
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:34,600
before we take Rory to the doctor, right?

24
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:36,880
When we know that we're about to take Rory to the doctor,

25
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:40,720
we use this title of doctor to prepare him.

26
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:43,060
We have a good doctor, right?

27
00:01:43,060 --> 00:01:46,360
Rory, tomorrow we are going to see Dr. Grant.

28
00:01:46,360 --> 00:01:49,000
Therefore, you know how to mentally prepare.

29
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:50,540
And he'll start pointing to his ear like,

30
00:01:50,540 --> 00:01:51,980
yep, he's gonna stick that thing in my ear.

31
00:01:51,980 --> 00:01:53,080
I know that's what's gonna happen.

32
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:55,900
Because the title helps prepare him for what's to come.

33
00:01:55,900 --> 00:01:58,880
And so in this list of titles that Isaiah gives us,

34
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:01,540
it is preparing us for what the Messiah is going to be

35
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:02,720
when he comes the first time,

36
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:04,860
what he's inviting us to participate in

37
00:02:04,860 --> 00:02:07,600
as we await for him to come the second time.

38
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:10,500
My hope is by the end of this short message,

39
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:11,540
I promise it will be short.

40
00:02:11,540 --> 00:02:13,840
I'm probably gonna stick to my notes far more

41
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:15,780
than I normally do because if I don't,

42
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:17,080
it will not be a short message.

43
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:20,000
So by the end of this message,

44
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,780
I hope that we can begin to better understand

45
00:02:22,780 --> 00:02:26,020
what it means for Jesus to be our wonderful counselor.

46
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:27,720
This is the first title we're gonna look at.

47
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:29,140
Can you look at your neighbor and say wonderful?

48
00:02:29,140 --> 00:02:33,080
Can you look at your other neighbor and say counselor?

49
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:37,980
Hopefully by the end of this message,

50
00:02:37,980 --> 00:02:39,600
we'll understand what it means for Jesus

51
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:40,780
to be our wonderful counselor

52
00:02:40,780 --> 00:02:42,800
and why that should give us hope.

53
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:47,980
This confident expectation that what Jesus says is true

54
00:02:47,980 --> 00:02:49,920
and we can hold tight to it.

55
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:50,260
Let's pray.

56
00:02:50,260 --> 00:02:52,380
Father in heaven, we love you

57
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:55,320
and we thank you for this wonderful family of God

58
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:59,880
that you have brought together under this one roof with floors.

59
00:02:59,880 --> 00:03:02,220
We are so grateful to be here

60
00:03:02,220 --> 00:03:06,000
and we just look forward to what you are going to do

61
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,360
and what you have already done

62
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:09,800
and what you're going to continue to do

63
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:11,180
through not just this service,

64
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:13,200
but through the family that we are becoming.

65
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:15,540
Because the church is so much more

66
00:03:15,540 --> 00:03:17,120
than what we do on Sunday mornings,

67
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:19,060
it's who we are throughout the week together

68
00:03:19,060 --> 00:03:20,180
in one another's lives.

69
00:03:20,180 --> 00:03:24,360
And so God, form in us your image for your glory.

70
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:26,320
It's in Jesus' name I pray, amen.

71
00:03:26,320 --> 00:03:28,880
All right, I tried to get the word out.

72
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:30,800
So hopefully as many of you as possible

73
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:33,200
were able to watch the episode of Bluey called The Creek.

74
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:35,200
Raise your hand if you were able to see it.

75
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:36,360
All right, awesome.

76
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:37,960
Many of you are there.

77
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:39,520
So for those of you that missed it,

78
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:42,300
I'm gonna try and do a quick recap of the episode.

79
00:03:42,440 --> 00:03:45,340
Bluey and her friends are playing on the playground,

80
00:03:45,340 --> 00:03:47,580
but they get bored.

81
00:03:47,580 --> 00:03:48,480
Imagine that.

82
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:51,340
Bluey wants her dad to play with her,

83
00:03:51,340 --> 00:03:53,220
but he's too big for the playground toys.

84
00:03:53,220 --> 00:03:54,720
Dad, she wants dad to play.

85
00:03:54,720 --> 00:03:56,020
Dad can't play on the playground

86
00:03:56,020 --> 00:03:57,020
because I mean, look at him.

87
00:03:57,020 --> 00:03:58,360
He's a bit chunky.

88
00:03:58,360 --> 00:03:59,700
He needs to go on a Christmas diet.

89
00:03:59,700 --> 00:04:00,260
It's fine.

90
00:04:00,260 --> 00:04:04,320
So he invites her, convinces her

91
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:06,240
that if she wants him to play with her,

92
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:08,440
they can walk down to the creek.

93
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:12,100
She's a bit nervous, a bit anxious about the trip,

94
00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:14,840
but eventually she gives in to her dad's advice.

95
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:18,160
It doesn't take long before she's changed her mind.

96
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:21,420
Spider webs, leeches, and sliding down hills.

97
00:04:21,420 --> 00:04:22,900
The path is more difficult

98
00:04:22,900 --> 00:04:24,660
than she ever could have anticipated.

99
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:27,320
The idea of the creek seemed more beautiful

100
00:04:27,320 --> 00:04:28,940
than the creek itself.

101
00:04:28,940 --> 00:04:30,720
And if you have, hopefully you have a coloring sheet.

102
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:32,220
We're gonna get to some notes on the back,

103
00:04:32,220 --> 00:04:32,860
just so you know.

104
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:34,680
We're gonna follow along there.

105
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:36,080
So she's pretty nervous.

106
00:04:36,080 --> 00:04:39,280
Obviously, spider webs and leeches

107
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:41,540
might make the most brave of us nervous,

108
00:04:41,540 --> 00:04:42,700
but her dad picks her up.

109
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:44,420
He encourages her to keep going

110
00:04:44,420 --> 00:04:46,640
and he goes before her.

111
00:04:46,640 --> 00:04:48,980
He knows the trip is doable

112
00:04:48,980 --> 00:04:50,720
and the reward is great

113
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:53,800
because as a kid, he has done this trip many times.

114
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:56,900
Finally, the hard work pays off

115
00:04:56,900 --> 00:04:59,380
as they arrive at the creek.

116
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:05,380
Bluey gasps, the creek is beautiful.

117
00:05:05,380 --> 00:05:09,860
And dad asks, do you want to go back to the playground?

118
00:05:09,860 --> 00:05:14,360
And Bluey explains, no, I like it here.

119
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:17,460
This episode, in my view,

120
00:05:17,460 --> 00:05:19,120
gives us a clear and beautiful picture

121
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:20,880
for how Jesus operates

122
00:05:20,880 --> 00:05:23,380
as the wonderful counselor in our lives.

123
00:05:23,380 --> 00:05:25,760
Jesus functions much like Bluey's father,

124
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:28,160
inviting us into a more beautiful image

125
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:29,920
of what creation really is,

126
00:05:29,920 --> 00:05:31,880
of what being a human is really like

127
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:34,360
than we could ever imagine on our own.

128
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:37,040
But it takes us following his counsel.

129
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:38,740
As the wonderful counselor,

130
00:05:38,740 --> 00:05:40,880
it takes us having the faith

131
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:42,540
to walk the difficult path

132
00:05:42,540 --> 00:05:45,460
that the father has laid out before us.

133
00:05:45,460 --> 00:05:49,060
And so in Isaiah chapter nine,

134
00:05:49,060 --> 00:05:51,840
we get this list of titles

135
00:05:51,840 --> 00:05:53,520
and it says,

136
00:05:53,660 --> 00:05:55,300
for a child is born to us.

137
00:05:55,300 --> 00:05:56,620
A son is given,

138
00:05:56,620 --> 00:05:58,660
the government shall rest on his shoulders

139
00:05:58,660 --> 00:06:01,620
and he will be called Wonderful Counselor,

140
00:06:01,620 --> 00:06:03,600
Mighty God, Everlasting Father,

141
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:04,700
Prince of Peace.

142
00:06:04,700 --> 00:06:06,920
The government and its peace will never end.

143
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:09,860
He will rule with fairness and justice

144
00:06:09,860 --> 00:06:11,580
from the throne of his ancestor David

145
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:12,400
for all eternity.

146
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:14,100
The passionate commitment

147
00:06:14,100 --> 00:06:15,620
of the Lord of Heaven's armies

148
00:06:15,620 --> 00:06:17,300
will make this happen.

149
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:18,920
So as we look at our notes

150
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:20,460
and we see this title

151
00:06:20,460 --> 00:06:21,880
of Wonderful Counselor,

152
00:06:21,880 --> 00:06:23,880
the Hebrew word for wonderful

153
00:06:23,880 --> 00:06:26,720
literally is too good to describe, right?

154
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:27,820
It's a placeholder word.

155
00:06:27,820 --> 00:06:28,640
It's a word saying,

156
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:29,960
we don't have a word

157
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:32,200
to be as good as the word we need,

158
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:34,000
so wonderful is the word we're gonna use.

159
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,840
Wonderful means too good

160
00:06:35,840 --> 00:06:37,120
to put into words.

161
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:38,080
This is the adjective

162
00:06:38,080 --> 00:06:40,000
that describes the type of counselor

163
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,820
that God is.

164
00:06:41,820 --> 00:06:42,940
And a counselor,

165
00:06:42,940 --> 00:06:43,820
what does a counselor do?

166
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:45,540
A counselor gives us direction

167
00:06:45,540 --> 00:06:47,700
that leads to joy.

168
00:06:47,700 --> 00:06:49,400
So if you have your notes,

169
00:06:49,400 --> 00:06:50,880
you can follow along with me.

170
00:06:50,880 --> 00:06:52,140
If you are an older kid

171
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:53,940
and your younger sibling

172
00:06:53,940 --> 00:06:55,940
maybe struggles with writing,

173
00:06:55,940 --> 00:06:57,400
would love for you to help them

174
00:06:57,400 --> 00:06:58,440
take notes,

175
00:06:58,440 --> 00:06:59,940
be a good example to them.

176
00:06:59,940 --> 00:07:01,020
Wonderful, too good

177
00:07:01,020 --> 00:07:02,840
to put into words counselor.

178
00:07:02,840 --> 00:07:03,800
It gives us direction

179
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:04,720
that leads to joy.

180
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:06,800
Now, I want us to notice

181
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:07,940
in this passage

182
00:07:07,940 --> 00:07:10,020
that when God sends Jesus

183
00:07:10,020 --> 00:07:11,720
to be our wonderful counselor,

184
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:14,500
he does so by sending a child.

185
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:17,140
Not a big, mighty warrior,

186
00:07:17,140 --> 00:07:19,520
but a small and humble child.

187
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:20,800
And so if you're in here

188
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:21,840
and you're a child,

189
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:23,440
I want you to hear

190
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:25,400
that God can and will use you

191
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:26,640
for his purposes now.

192
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:28,880
You do not need to wait

193
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:29,760
until you get bigger

194
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:30,580
to know God

195
00:07:30,580 --> 00:07:31,760
and work alongside him.

196
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:33,680
He is inviting you to do so now.

197
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:34,140
And actually,

198
00:07:34,140 --> 00:07:35,280
there's stories in the gospel

199
00:07:35,280 --> 00:07:36,080
where it seems like

200
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:37,600
he wants all of the adults

201
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:38,380
to come to him

202
00:07:38,380 --> 00:07:39,520
like you all come to him.

203
00:07:40,060 --> 00:07:41,460
And so please know

204
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:42,500
that you are invited

205
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:43,260
to participate

206
00:07:43,260 --> 00:07:44,020
in a relationship

207
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:44,720
with the creator

208
00:07:44,720 --> 00:07:45,400
of the universe.

209
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:47,160
He is your wonderful counselor.

210
00:07:47,160 --> 00:07:49,040
He wants to give you advice

211
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:50,220
that leads to joy.

212
00:07:50,220 --> 00:07:51,320
And you can begin

213
00:07:51,320 --> 00:07:53,120
walking that path now.

214
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:55,420
You can avoid lots of problems

215
00:07:55,420 --> 00:07:56,120
and difficulties

216
00:07:56,120 --> 00:07:57,020
that many of us

217
00:07:57,020 --> 00:07:57,820
have stepped into

218
00:07:57,820 --> 00:07:59,620
because we weren't following Jesus

219
00:07:59,620 --> 00:08:00,780
as our wonderful counselor.

220
00:08:00,780 --> 00:08:03,340
Adults, our children,

221
00:08:03,340 --> 00:08:04,800
and this,

222
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:05,820
I'm talking to those of you

223
00:08:05,820 --> 00:08:07,640
that even if you don't have children,

224
00:08:07,780 --> 00:08:08,580
all of the children

225
00:08:08,580 --> 00:08:10,000
that are a part of our church

226
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,780
are not just the church of tomorrow.

227
00:08:11,780 --> 00:08:13,140
They are the church of today

228
00:08:13,140 --> 00:08:14,380
and they need all of us,

229
00:08:14,380 --> 00:08:15,680
parents and not parents,

230
00:08:15,680 --> 00:08:17,800
to encourage and equip them

231
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:19,600
in their relationship with him.

232
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:22,340
Jesus comes as a child

233
00:08:22,340 --> 00:08:23,820
to be the savior of the world.

234
00:08:23,820 --> 00:08:25,740
And as the savior of the world,

235
00:08:25,740 --> 00:08:27,860
he is our wonderful counselor

236
00:08:27,860 --> 00:08:29,760
that gives us direction

237
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:31,860
that leads to joy.

238
00:08:32,500 --> 00:08:34,380
So, first point in the notes,

239
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:37,320
I think is this,

240
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:39,000
that Jesus tells us

241
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,440
the direction we should go.

242
00:08:40,440 --> 00:08:42,420
Jesus, as our wonderful counselor,

243
00:08:42,420 --> 00:08:44,520
announces to us

244
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:45,820
the direction that we should go.

245
00:08:45,820 --> 00:08:47,140
As our wonderful counselor,

246
00:08:47,140 --> 00:08:49,560
he declares this is the way to go.

247
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:51,260
He declares I am the way,

248
00:08:51,260 --> 00:08:52,560
the truth, and the life.

249
00:08:52,560 --> 00:08:54,480
Anyone who would come to the Father

250
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:57,280
must come by me,

251
00:08:57,280 --> 00:08:58,440
by following me,

252
00:08:58,440 --> 00:09:01,120
by taking my advice.

253
00:09:02,120 --> 00:09:06,540
And if you've ever had the experience

254
00:09:06,540 --> 00:09:07,800
of going to a counselor,

255
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:10,220
some of you maybe have had good counselors,

256
00:09:10,220 --> 00:09:11,920
some of you have had bad counselors,

257
00:09:11,920 --> 00:09:15,860
but the best counselors give good direction.

258
00:09:15,860 --> 00:09:18,620
They look at the circumstances of your life,

259
00:09:18,620 --> 00:09:20,920
the situations that you have experienced,

260
00:09:20,920 --> 00:09:21,520
the things,

261
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:23,160
the behaviors that you have developed

262
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:24,300
through those experiences,

263
00:09:24,300 --> 00:09:25,860
and they tell you

264
00:09:25,860 --> 00:09:27,000
where you're believing things

265
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:27,580
that aren't true.

266
00:09:27,580 --> 00:09:30,000
And they invite you

267
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,280
into a different direction

268
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:33,860
that will ultimately lead to more joy.

269
00:09:33,860 --> 00:09:36,780
I've had a good counselor in my life,

270
00:09:36,780 --> 00:09:38,280
and this is what he does for me.

271
00:09:38,280 --> 00:09:40,420
He asks me good questions.

272
00:09:40,420 --> 00:09:42,080
He examines my circumstances

273
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:43,040
and my behaviors,

274
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:44,480
and he invites me to go

275
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:45,860
in a different direction

276
00:09:45,860 --> 00:09:47,680
that leads to joy.

277
00:09:47,680 --> 00:09:48,660
Good counselors,

278
00:09:48,660 --> 00:09:49,740
the best counselors,

279
00:09:49,740 --> 00:09:51,440
they study how the brain works,

280
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:53,600
how the body interacts with the world,

281
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:55,820
and they can see when something is wrong

282
00:09:55,820 --> 00:09:58,400
and help us move in the right direction.

283
00:09:58,400 --> 00:10:01,420
But Jesus isn't just a good counselor.

284
00:10:01,420 --> 00:10:03,860
He's a wonderful one.

285
00:10:03,860 --> 00:10:05,620
Too good for words.

286
00:10:05,620 --> 00:10:07,720
He doesn't have to study our body

287
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:09,580
and our brains because he created them.

288
00:10:09,580 --> 00:10:12,320
He made you unique in your mother's womb,

289
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:14,860
and he knows the direction you need to go

290
00:10:14,860 --> 00:10:17,180
in order to experience joy.

291
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:19,940
Jesus, the wonderful counselor,

292
00:10:19,940 --> 00:10:23,320
gives good advice that leads to joy.

293
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:25,480
In one of his most well-known sermons

294
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:27,000
in Matthew chapter five through seven

295
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:28,420
called the Sermon on the Mount,

296
00:10:28,420 --> 00:10:30,180
he spends time doing this.

297
00:10:30,180 --> 00:10:32,080
He spends time telling people

298
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:33,620
the direction that they should go.

299
00:10:33,620 --> 00:10:35,500
He starts with phrases like,

300
00:10:35,660 --> 00:10:36,600
you have heard it said,

301
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:40,820
or everyone around you believes this thing,

302
00:10:40,820 --> 00:10:42,980
but I say to you.

303
00:10:42,980 --> 00:10:45,060
So he starts with something we all believe,

304
00:10:45,060 --> 00:10:46,480
and as a wonderful counselor,

305
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:46,800
he says,

306
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:48,360
let me give you some better advice

307
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:49,980
that ultimately leads to the life

308
00:10:49,980 --> 00:10:51,600
that I'm inviting you to.

309
00:10:51,600 --> 00:10:54,320
You have heard it said,

310
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:56,620
an eye for an eye and a tooth for a tooth,

311
00:10:56,620 --> 00:10:57,540
but I say to you,

312
00:10:57,540 --> 00:10:59,160
if someone slaps you on the cheek,

313
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:01,960
you should turn to them the other cheek.

314
00:11:03,460 --> 00:11:05,240
This is Jesus functioning

315
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:06,580
as our wonderful counselor,

316
00:11:06,580 --> 00:11:08,180
telling us the way that we should go,

317
00:11:08,180 --> 00:11:11,800
and the way that we should go is difficult, right?

318
00:11:11,800 --> 00:11:14,700
It's much easier when someone punches you

319
00:11:14,700 --> 00:11:15,760
to punch them back.

320
00:11:15,760 --> 00:11:18,380
Isn't that the thing that we all want to do

321
00:11:18,380 --> 00:11:19,100
when we get hit,

322
00:11:19,100 --> 00:11:20,020
or when we get slapped,

323
00:11:20,020 --> 00:11:21,240
or when we get made fun of,

324
00:11:21,240 --> 00:11:22,380
or when we get pushed down,

325
00:11:22,380 --> 00:11:24,520
the thing that we want to do is push back.

326
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:25,680
We wanna get up,

327
00:11:25,680 --> 00:11:26,700
and we wanna fight harder.

328
00:11:26,700 --> 00:11:29,000
We wanna take the pain that they've caused us

329
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:30,460
and cause them more pain,

330
00:11:30,460 --> 00:11:31,320
but Jesus says,

331
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:32,960
if you wanna experience true life,

332
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:34,500
the life that I've created you for,

333
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:36,420
the way that you experience that

334
00:11:36,420 --> 00:11:38,720
is not by doing what everyone else says.

335
00:11:38,720 --> 00:11:39,660
You have heard it said.

336
00:11:39,660 --> 00:11:40,820
Someone hits you,

337
00:11:40,820 --> 00:11:41,380
you hit back,

338
00:11:41,380 --> 00:11:42,240
but I say to you,

339
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:43,340
you turn the other cheek.

340
00:11:43,340 --> 00:11:49,120
He goes on,

341
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:50,260
you have heard it said,

342
00:11:50,260 --> 00:11:51,880
love your neighbor and hate your enemy.

343
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:54,500
This is somewhat wise advice, right?

344
00:11:54,500 --> 00:11:55,800
Love the people that are around you

345
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:56,960
that can benefit you,

346
00:11:56,960 --> 00:11:58,320
and anybody that comes after you

347
00:11:58,320 --> 00:11:59,040
or attacks you,

348
00:11:59,040 --> 00:12:01,080
attack them back.

349
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:02,320
But I say to you,

350
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:03,400
love your enemies

351
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:05,980
and pray for those who persecute you.

352
00:12:05,980 --> 00:12:08,780
Jesus takes worldly wisdom,

353
00:12:08,780 --> 00:12:09,580
advice.

354
00:12:09,580 --> 00:12:12,160
This is playground living, right?

355
00:12:12,160 --> 00:12:14,480
This is how we live and interact with people

356
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:16,140
apart from a relationship with God.

357
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:17,240
Bluey on the playground

358
00:12:17,240 --> 00:12:19,040
without her father's input.

359
00:12:19,040 --> 00:12:20,420
It's fine for a while.

360
00:12:20,420 --> 00:12:21,160
It might work,

361
00:12:21,480 --> 00:12:22,520
but eventually it will,

362
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:24,240
the joy will run out.

363
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:26,480
And the only place

364
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:28,420
where we can ultimately find full joy

365
00:12:28,420 --> 00:12:29,640
is to run to the father

366
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:30,840
for the relationship

367
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:31,880
that we were created to.

368
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:33,260
And when we look to him,

369
00:12:33,260 --> 00:12:33,640
he says,

370
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:34,640
you have heard it said,

371
00:12:34,640 --> 00:12:36,780
hate your enemy,

372
00:12:36,780 --> 00:12:37,420
but I say,

373
00:12:37,420 --> 00:12:38,840
love your enemy

374
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:40,060
and pray for those

375
00:12:40,060 --> 00:12:41,520
who persecute you.

376
00:12:41,520 --> 00:12:41,760
Just,

377
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:44,860
I just want you for just a second

378
00:12:44,860 --> 00:12:46,420
to imagine the type of world

379
00:12:46,420 --> 00:12:47,400
that would be created

380
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:48,960
if God's people,

381
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:50,420
if all of God's people

382
00:12:50,420 --> 00:12:53,060
actually lived the words of Jesus.

383
00:12:53,060 --> 00:12:55,280
If we actually viewed him

384
00:12:55,280 --> 00:12:56,220
as the wonderful counselor,

385
00:12:56,220 --> 00:12:58,300
if we actually viewed his voice,

386
00:12:58,300 --> 00:13:00,320
his advice as advice

387
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:01,840
that leads us to deeper joy.

388
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:03,020
Imagine the type of world

389
00:13:03,020 --> 00:13:03,680
that we would create

390
00:13:03,680 --> 00:13:05,300
when every time somebody hits us,

391
00:13:05,300 --> 00:13:07,680
we pray

392
00:13:07,680 --> 00:13:10,400
and we ask God's blessing

393
00:13:10,400 --> 00:13:11,180
on those people.

394
00:13:11,180 --> 00:13:15,420
Sounds very difficult, Eliza.

395
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:16,900
You are so right.

396
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:18,860
And that is why

397
00:13:18,860 --> 00:13:20,820
following Jesus is hard,

398
00:13:20,820 --> 00:13:21,680
but ultimately,

399
00:13:21,680 --> 00:13:22,840
it is the way

400
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:24,320
that we should go.

401
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:25,380
The playground's easy.

402
00:13:25,380 --> 00:13:26,880
The creek is beautiful.

403
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:29,820
It's what we've been invited to.

404
00:13:29,820 --> 00:13:32,620
Because Jesus

405
00:13:32,620 --> 00:13:34,180
is the wonderful counselor, Eliza,

406
00:13:34,180 --> 00:13:35,240
he doesn't just tell us

407
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:36,500
what we should do,

408
00:13:36,500 --> 00:13:38,740
but he gives us an example.

409
00:13:38,740 --> 00:13:41,240
He gives us the direction.

410
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:44,480
Second point in our notes

411
00:13:44,480 --> 00:13:46,520
is that Jesus leads the way.

412
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:49,700
The direction that Jesus invites us to

413
00:13:49,700 --> 00:13:50,780
is hard to hear.

414
00:13:50,780 --> 00:13:54,260
He knows that this is a scary invitation.

415
00:13:54,260 --> 00:13:57,820
He doesn't just tell us

416
00:13:57,820 --> 00:14:00,020
what to do from afar,

417
00:14:00,020 --> 00:14:02,520
but he gets down dirty with us.

418
00:14:02,520 --> 00:14:04,100
That's what Advent is all about.

419
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:06,700
That Jesus was born a little baby.

420
00:14:06,700 --> 00:14:09,060
That he experienced enemies

421
00:14:09,060 --> 00:14:11,200
hitting him and slapping him

422
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:12,100
and making fun of him.

423
00:14:12,140 --> 00:14:14,060
That he experienced all the pain

424
00:14:14,060 --> 00:14:14,900
and difficulty

425
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:16,100
that you and I will face.

426
00:14:16,100 --> 00:14:18,660
And in experiencing that,

427
00:14:18,660 --> 00:14:19,560
he doesn't just say,

428
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:20,280
love your enemies,

429
00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:22,360
but he actually does it before us.

430
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:23,740
He goes before us.

431
00:14:23,740 --> 00:14:25,040
He shows us an example.

432
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:26,240
He accomplishes the thing

433
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:27,400
that we could never accomplish

434
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:29,020
because it is too hard for us to do.

435
00:14:29,020 --> 00:14:31,480
And he invites us

436
00:14:31,480 --> 00:14:34,200
to imperfectly follow behind his example.

437
00:14:34,920 --> 00:14:37,120
To receive the grace and forgiveness

438
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:38,020
that he gives us.

439
00:14:38,020 --> 00:14:40,340
Jesus doesn't just tell us

440
00:14:40,340 --> 00:14:42,120
not to repay evil with evil.

441
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:42,980
He shows us.

442
00:14:42,980 --> 00:14:44,540
He doesn't just tell us

443
00:14:44,540 --> 00:14:45,680
to love our enemies.

444
00:14:45,680 --> 00:14:46,600
He shows us.

445
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:48,840
Jesus went to the cross

446
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:50,640
to show us the ultimate example.

447
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:52,580
He loved us

448
00:14:52,580 --> 00:14:54,180
even when we were his enemies.

449
00:14:54,180 --> 00:14:58,120
And even on the cross,

450
00:14:58,120 --> 00:14:59,940
as his enemies were doing

451
00:14:59,940 --> 00:15:01,260
the worst possible thing

452
00:15:01,260 --> 00:15:02,820
that anyone could do to anyone,

453
00:15:03,540 --> 00:15:04,580
something that none of us

454
00:15:04,580 --> 00:15:05,400
have experienced,

455
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:08,000
he looked up to the heavens

456
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:09,240
and he prayed to the Father,

457
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:10,440
Father, forgive them

458
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:11,440
for they do not know

459
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:12,200
what they are doing.

460
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:14,120
Jesus is our wonderful counselor

461
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:15,460
who both tells us

462
00:15:15,460 --> 00:15:16,860
the direction that leads to life

463
00:15:16,860 --> 00:15:18,780
and shows us the way.

464
00:15:18,780 --> 00:15:21,840
And even though

465
00:15:21,840 --> 00:15:22,960
it's the most complicated,

466
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:24,340
difficult invitation

467
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:25,540
that you could ever imagine,

468
00:15:25,540 --> 00:15:29,420
he gave us this anchoring point,

469
00:15:29,420 --> 00:15:30,180
this lighthouse

470
00:15:30,180 --> 00:15:31,340
in the midst of the storm.

471
00:15:32,020 --> 00:15:33,020
And that lighthouse

472
00:15:33,020 --> 00:15:34,360
is the resurrection.

473
00:15:34,360 --> 00:15:36,480
The resurrection proves

474
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:37,500
that the way of Jesus

475
00:15:37,500 --> 00:15:39,240
is the way that leads to victory

476
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:40,860
and all other ways will fail.

477
00:15:40,860 --> 00:15:43,400
Fighting back against your enemy,

478
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:45,120
doing what the world does,

479
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:46,580
it might work for a while,

480
00:15:46,580 --> 00:15:48,160
it might be easier in the moment,

481
00:15:48,160 --> 00:15:49,360
but it will fail.

482
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:50,780
The resurrection proves

483
00:15:50,780 --> 00:15:51,620
the only time

484
00:15:51,620 --> 00:15:53,660
that anyone's death

485
00:15:53,660 --> 00:15:54,580
wasn't eternal

486
00:15:54,580 --> 00:15:56,320
was when they lived

487
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:58,100
this perfect way of being.

488
00:15:59,140 --> 00:16:00,080
And Jesus says,

489
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:01,100
if you want to have victory,

490
00:16:01,100 --> 00:16:02,860
if you want to have eternal life,

491
00:16:02,860 --> 00:16:04,440
if you want to experience

492
00:16:04,440 --> 00:16:06,140
the beauty of the kingdom of God

493
00:16:06,140 --> 00:16:07,200
before I return

494
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:08,560
and all of the plowshares

495
00:16:08,560 --> 00:16:09,920
will be beat into,

496
00:16:09,920 --> 00:16:11,020
or all of the swords

497
00:16:11,020 --> 00:16:12,120
will be beat into plowshares,

498
00:16:12,120 --> 00:16:12,900
if you want to begin

499
00:16:12,900 --> 00:16:14,140
to experience the life

500
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:15,260
of the kingdom of God now,

501
00:16:15,260 --> 00:16:16,560
you follow me.

502
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:22,100
We often get tricked

503
00:16:22,100 --> 00:16:22,780
into believing

504
00:16:22,780 --> 00:16:23,980
that we can have true life

505
00:16:23,980 --> 00:16:25,280
by following our own way

506
00:16:25,280 --> 00:16:26,800
and it will work for a while,

507
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:28,860
but eventually it will stop

508
00:16:28,860 --> 00:16:31,900
because ultimately

509
00:16:31,900 --> 00:16:32,460
we were made

510
00:16:32,460 --> 00:16:33,820
for a relationship with God.

511
00:16:33,820 --> 00:16:34,520
It's just like Bluey

512
00:16:34,520 --> 00:16:35,060
on the playground,

513
00:16:35,060 --> 00:16:37,180
life without her dad.

514
00:16:37,180 --> 00:16:38,960
It's good for a while,

515
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:40,520
but ultimately it runs out

516
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:41,880
and she runs to the father

517
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:42,140
and says,

518
00:16:42,140 --> 00:16:43,500
I want to play with you,

519
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:45,840
but if you want to play with him,

520
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:47,240
you've got to go where he goes

521
00:16:47,240 --> 00:16:49,080
and he can't be where we are.

522
00:16:49,140 --> 00:16:50,940
He is in the kingdom of God

523
00:16:50,940 --> 00:16:52,000
and that is what we are invited

524
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:52,900
to participate in.

525
00:16:52,900 --> 00:16:54,140
The path is difficult

526
00:16:54,140 --> 00:16:55,960
and we will often be tempted

527
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:56,640
to turn around.

528
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:58,480
There are leeches

529
00:16:58,480 --> 00:16:59,760
and spider webs

530
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:01,460
and slippery slopes

531
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:03,160
on the way of Jesus.

532
00:17:03,160 --> 00:17:04,840
The road is narrow

533
00:17:04,840 --> 00:17:06,620
that leads to life.

534
00:17:06,620 --> 00:17:07,480
It is difficult.

535
00:17:07,480 --> 00:17:09,700
No one is going to tell you

536
00:17:09,700 --> 00:17:11,440
differently from this pulpit

537
00:17:11,440 --> 00:17:12,240
and if they do,

538
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:15,260
thank you.

539
00:17:15,260 --> 00:17:16,600
Don't trust them.

540
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:17,160
There we go.

541
00:17:17,160 --> 00:17:18,260
Don't trust me.

542
00:17:19,140 --> 00:17:20,160
The path is difficult.

543
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:21,340
We will often be tempted

544
00:17:21,340 --> 00:17:21,940
to turn around,

545
00:17:21,940 --> 00:17:23,120
but true life is found

546
00:17:23,120 --> 00:17:24,000
in following Jesus

547
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:24,820
no matter how hard

548
00:17:24,820 --> 00:17:25,580
the path gets.

549
00:17:25,580 --> 00:17:26,780
So,

550
00:17:26,780 --> 00:17:29,580
have you made this decision

551
00:17:29,580 --> 00:17:31,420
to follow Jesus

552
00:17:31,420 --> 00:17:33,180
as your wonderful counselor

553
00:17:33,180 --> 00:17:34,760
who both tells us

554
00:17:34,760 --> 00:17:36,180
the way that leads us to joy

555
00:17:36,180 --> 00:17:37,380
and shows us

556
00:17:37,380 --> 00:17:38,460
the way that we should live?

557
00:17:38,460 --> 00:17:42,500
Are we focused on following him

558
00:17:42,500 --> 00:17:44,120
and embodying his way

559
00:17:44,120 --> 00:17:45,440
of being in the world?

560
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:47,760
Or are we getting distracted

561
00:17:47,760 --> 00:17:48,640
by the difficulty

562
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:49,700
of the road?

563
00:17:49,700 --> 00:17:51,860
The invitation this morning

564
00:17:51,860 --> 00:17:54,240
as we remember

565
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:55,400
Christ's first coming

566
00:17:55,400 --> 00:17:56,140
and anticipate

567
00:17:56,140 --> 00:17:57,140
his second coming

568
00:17:57,140 --> 00:17:59,800
is to view his advice

569
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:00,700
and his example

570
00:18:00,700 --> 00:18:02,540
as the path

571
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:03,120
to follow

572
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:05,840
as a wonderful counselor.

573
00:18:05,840 --> 00:18:06,940
Hebrews chapter 12

574
00:18:06,940 --> 00:18:07,720
verses 1 and 2

575
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:08,500
says it this way.

576
00:18:09,180 --> 00:18:10,480
